      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 11: 🟡 The compiler guard `defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)` is too broad for the Windows/MSVC family: `clang-cl` defines `__clang__` but still follows MSVC frontend constraints where GNU-style inline asm is not supported on ARM/AArch64. This can reintroduce the same build failure for clang-cl targets. Please gate these asm branches with an explicit MSVC exclusion (e.g. `!defined(_MSC_VER)`) or with a positive check for GNU-style asm support so both `ReadStatusWord()` and `SetStatusWord()` are safe across Windows ARM toolchains.",
